Ran all 6 verify-phase checks from the plan against the live ~/bob vault:
(1) all inbound [[podcasts#^...]] anchors across the vault resolve in the new podcasts.md — 0 missing;
(2) diffed backup URLs (/tmp/bob_modernize_backup/{quote,podcasts}.md) against the rewritten set — 0 lost URLs in either file;
(3) every [[wikilink]] target in quote.md, podcasts.md, podcast.md, and podcasts/*.md resolves to an existing .md/.base file;
(4) podcasts.base parses under yaml.safe_load, and 'bob query TABLE ... FROM "podcasts" WHERE type = [[podcast]]' returns exactly the 15 expected notes (9 status=subscribed, 6 status=unsubscribed) — confirmed the data layer the 4 Base views render from; no headless Obsidian renderer available in this environment to visually confirm the .base embed, matching the same limitation f.1 hit;
(5) frontmatter on all 17 new/changed notes plus quote.md/podcasts.md parses with quoted-wikilink parent/type, and type: "[[podcast]]" resolves to podcast.md;
(6) git -C ~/bob status --short shows exactly M quote.md, M podcasts.md, M mind.md (diff is the single added '- [[podcasts]]' line), ?? podcast.md, ?? podcasts.base, ?? podcasts/, plus a baseline of other M/?? files (bob.md, body.md, cash.md, dev.md, gtd_daily.md, job.md, love.md, sase.md, sase_blog_0.md, 2026/20260805.md, 2026/20260806.md) all confirmed pre-existing via mtimes earlier than the epic's 07:33:58 creation time. Nothing staged or committed.
Also confirmed: quote.md has 32 callouts/32 human-slug block IDs and zero self-referential ^z- anchors (the 10 remaining ^z- occurrences are all outbound refs to other notes' anchors, explicitly required verbatim by the plan); podcasts.md carries all 17 original ^z- anchors exactly once each; no zorg_*/ID::/LID::/====== / NNNNNN#XX scaffolding remains in quote.md or podcasts.md (zorg_id fields and ## Source fences in podcasts/*.md are intentional per plan schema, not leftovers). Epic acceptance criteria fully met.
